AD  - American University Of Ras Al Khaimah, Dept Of Computer Science And Engineering, Ras al Khaimah, United Arab Emirates
AB  - Serious games are engaging software simulations aimed at promoting practical learning within the health, education, and cultural sectors. These tools allow users to enhance their knowledge, skills, and behavioral competencies through handson training experiences. This systematic review investigates the evolving use of serious games, emphasizing their design strategies, development processes, and evaluation approaches. We tackle two essential research questions by thoroughly analyzing 44 peerreviewed articles obtained from IEEE Xplore, ScienceDirect, Springer, ACM Digital Library, and Google Scholar. Our results indicate notable shifts in evaluation methods, with questionnaire assessments and pre-/post-test protocols becoming the primary validation strategies. A comparative review of prior literature underscores advancements specific to various domains, especially within educational and healthcare applications. The synthesis presents empirically grounded guidance for scholars and professionals on the design, deployment, and evaluation of serious games across various domains. © 2026 IEEE.
