AB  - This paper presents an empirical study at the intersection of computing and education. It aims to investigate the impact mechanism of Generative Artificial Intelligence (AIGC), as an emerging computing technology, on university students’ learning engagement through the affordances of its learning environment. Grounded in affordance theory, the study constructs and validates a chain mediation model. By analyzing questionnaire data from university students using Structural Equation Modeling, the findings reveal that the utilitarian, hedonic, and technological affordances of AIGC not only directly and positively influence learning engagement but also exert an indirect effect on it through the mediating variable of learning self-efficacy. This research elucidates the intrinsic mechanism within the human-AI collaborative learning environment via the “technological features - psychological perception - behavioral performance” pathway. It provides crucial interdisciplinary theoretical foundations and insights for algorithmic optimization to facilitate the deep integration and adaptive system design of AIGC in educational contexts. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
