AB  - University students’ major adaptation refers to the ability of students to proactively adjust themselves—based on their fundamental competencies and personality traits—through interactions with their chosen discipline and its environment, in order to achieve a balance between internal and external academic conditions that is conducive to favorable development. Good professional adaptability can promote the training of college students and the development of higher education. Conventional research mainly explores the influencing factors of major adaptability through questionnaire surveys and statistical analysis, lacking dynamic evaluation and personalized optimization mechanisms. This paper uses AI-based graph neural network technology to construct a major adaptability assessment tool, models data such as major commitment, major learning goals, major learning behaviors, major self-efficacy, and major external environment of students from different majors in 10 universities, and effectively identifies important factors affecting professional adaptability. An analysis of influencing factors was conducted based on the assessment results. The results showed that the dynamic adaptive optimization tool driven by graph neural network can support personalized academic planning and the Intelligent development of higher education. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s)
