AB  - The development of AI Generated Content (AIGC), which is seen as an example of increasing at a spectacular pace, has brought digital changes in industry and brings out with new form education worldwide. In China the modernization of vocational education becomes the focus for the implementation of the 14th FYP, where it was highlighted the integration of smart technologies in reform of curriculum.The goal of this paper is to investigate the new model of the AIGC-based machine learning-guided intelligent fashion design curriculum development in higher vocational education which helps students strengthen their computer digital capability, creativeness and other workplace competencies. In this way, K-Means cluster analysis (a traditional unsupervised machine learning algorithm) is employed for the current paper to analyse data of the 200 survey questionnaires of students' attitude toward AIGC based curriculum reform.The behavioral and attitudinal latent patterns are determined using clustering of learners, with behavioral and design competency features used to group learners. Validation statistics, specifically the Elbow Method, Silhouette Coefficient, and Davies-Bouldin Index found three clusters to best balance interpretability and stability for model fitting.Findings can distinguish three types of audiences' attitude - conservative, moderate and very supporting - towards the application of AIGC technology, providing meaningful evidence to differentiate curriculum development. The analysis proves that integrating AIGC applications and K-Means algorithm supports data-driven, adaptive and evidence-informed education, career and skills development in vocational education, as well as better matching training and industry demands.This work is therefore considered to make a contribution to a reproducible system of intelligent curriculum reformation to back the digital and green revolution of the fashion design education system in China.  © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
