TI  - Triple-Dimension Integration Teaching Model for Web Design Courses: Industry-University Collaboration Oriented Reform and Validation
PY  - 2026
T2  - Proceedings of 2025 3rd International Conference on Information Education and Artificial Intelligence, ICIEAI 2025
SP  - 1184
EP  - 1192
DO  - 10.1145/3799457.3799651
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105040169327?origin=resultslist
AD  - Guangzhou University of Software, Guangdong, Guangzhou, China
AB  - To address the disconnection between web design course teaching, student cognitive development, and industry practical demands, this study proposes a Triple-Dimension Integration (TDI) teaching model integrating technical proficiency, cognitive competence, and industrial adaptability. Taking 88 second-year Network Technology majors at Guangzhou University of Software as research objects, a convergent parallel mixed-methods design was adopted (2024-2025). Quantitative data included course project scores, industry competency tests, and student skill questionnaires; qualitative data came from interviews with 4 teachers, 3 industry experts, and 8 students. To enhance the engineering and empirical rigor, additional mathematical modeling (AHP-Entropy weight method for evaluation index optimization), engineering analysis (enterprise cooperative project case), and multivariate statistical analysis (regression and correlation verification) were incorporated. Results show that the TDI model significantly improves student performance (overall score mean increased from 73.5 to 82.3, p<0.05), enhances industry demand matching rate (from 62% to 89%), and reduces learning barriers (technical application difficulties decreased by 41%). The structural equation model (SEM) verification shows the model's goodness-of-fit (χ2/df=2.31, RMSEA=0.068, CFI=0.92), confirming its validity. The model realizes the organic integration of knowledge teaching, ability training, and industry connection, providing a feasible reform path for web design course optimization in application-oriented universities.  © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
