AD  - School of International Business, Beijing University of Financial Technology, Beijing, China
AD  - Academic Affairs Office, Beijing University of Financial Technology, Beijing, China
AB  - In the context of rapid digital transformation in global business education, the integration of artificial intelligence (AI) with traditional business disciplines has emerged as a critical pathway for cultivating interdisciplinary talents. This study addresses the fragmentation of AI applications in accounting and finance curricula, proposing a three-tiered “1+2+3” AI-enabled curriculum model tailored for business studies. The model consists of 1 general education course for AI literacy, 2 technical courses for tool proficiency, and 3 categories of practical courses for scenario-based integration. To assess its effectiveness, we collected questionnaire data and applied a supervised machine learning Random Forest Regressor (RFR) and SHapley Additive exPlanations (SHAP). RFR is used to model the relationship between the input features and satisfaction. SHAP quantified global and local feature contributions and exposing the factors that most strongly influence satisfaction. The performance of the model is validated using percentage split method and evaluated using R2 and mean absolute error (MAE). Empirical results demonstrate that the model effectively enhances students’ AI competence and professional skills, providing a replicable paradigm for “AI+Business” curriculum reform. The study contributes to both theoretical frameworks of AI-empowered education and practical applications in integrating cutting-edge technologies with business core processes. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s)
