AB  - The quality of service provided by an institution providing higher education programs such as Undergraduate and Postgraduate courses often mean a lot for the overall competence and rankings of the institute or university. Maintaining high standards of service delivery is therefore very important for the institution. Since the past few decades substantial researches and studies have been conducted for improvising in service quality delivered and therein new standardized tools have been developed for the same. This study validates the HEdPERF scale in the context of a premium engineering college of Delhi, India with data collected for the research being limited to only undergraduate respondents. The research also concludes and effectively gives suggestions for attenuating in the service performance of the institution. The standard questionnaire for validation of the HEdPERF scale is selected and 113 technical undergraduates from various branches, years and demographic diversity are surveyed. Various statistical techniques such as gap value analysis between the student’s expectation and perception are done through the use of SPSS software. The analysis reveals a negative gap value towards almost all factors influencing service delivery such as academic and administrative staff co-operation, curriculum and programs offered etc. Towards the conclusion of the study, remedies have been suggested to improvise on the gap values obtained between the expectations and perceptions of the college’s undergraduates in respect to quality of service performance delivered by the institute. © INDIACom-2017.
